From 701378d9d3afecf77aafe53d1e9f69ad81139081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 05:17:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 37/49] x86_64/fpu/587: drop the x87 functions i386 retired

i386 replaced these x87 implementations by generic C or builtins (ceil,
floor and trunc raised Inexact, the float functions lacked the underflow
and errno handling of the current code).  Use the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
